  "primary_subject_agency_ids": [],
  "summary": "A new Grand Theft Auto V mod called 'Grand Theft Automated License Plate Reader' by artist Morry Kolman places 235 Flock ALPR cameras around Los Santos, letting players destroy them for $600 each and simulating police responses triggered by the cameras. The article frames the mod amid real-world vandalism of Flock cameras and mentions the LAPD's suspension of Flock use and 131 Flock contract terminations in August.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The mod installs 235 Flock cameras around the fictional Los Santos, a riff on the real-life city of Los Angeles.",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    },
    {
      "quote": "An NPR analysis found that Flock cameras have been vandalized in at least 36 states.",
      "paragraph_idx": 16
    },
    {
      "quote": "In real-life LA, the Los Angeles Police Department suspended its use of Flock cameras this summer following a recommendation from the LAPD's inspector general.",
      "paragraph_idx": 21
    },
    {
      "quote": "across the US, there were 131 Flock contract terminations in August alone, according to the anti-surveillance advocacy group Secure Justice",
      "paragraph_idx": 21
    }
  ],
